\title{Finite extensions are algebraic}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\ul{
\li{\strong{(i)} We have #{[K(\alpha):K] < \infty \iff \alpha} algebraic over #{K}.}
\li{\strong{(ii)} If #{[L:K] < \infty} then for any #{\alpha \in L} we certainly have #{[K(\alpha):K] < \infty}.}
}

\p{So any finite extension is algebraic, but the converse is false.}
